    "body": "This allows the user to set a minimum width for signature and info windows. If width_min isn't explicitly set, the default behavior is retained.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n  window = {\r\n    info = {... width_min = 6 },\r\n    signature = { ... width_min = 10 },\r\n  },\r\n```\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-03-06T11:29:55Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nI am afraid, this is a bit too much for 'mini.completion'. Otherwise it opens a pass to a slippery slope of various dedicated small scoped options.\r\n\r\nCurrently 'mini.completion' provides dedicated [events](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-completion.html#minicompletion-events) which should be enough to customize information and signature windows in any way users prefer. Including setting minimum width.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
